wo spot bitcoin exchange-traded funds on Wednesday, clearing products from two local asset managers to list on the Saudi Exchange (Tadawul), according to a notice published by the regulator. The CMA had not included crypto funds in its published product roadmap, so the approval came earlier than market participants expected. The funds will hold bitcoin directly and begin trading on November 20. The issuers said they plan to seed the funds with about 3,000 BTC bought on the spot market before launch. A CMA spokesperson confirmed the approval to The Block.\",\"title\":\"Saudi Arabia's Capital Market Authority approves first spot bitcoin ETFs for Tadawul; 3,000 BTC seed\",\"url\":\"https://www.theblock.co/news/regulation/2026-10-21-saudi-cma-approves-first-spot-bitcoin-etfs-tadawul-421342\"},\"message\":{\"item_id\":\"ITM-01M5EDBQP49XS17T5JW8FD0WFZ\",\"kind\":\"NEW_ITEM\"}}", "type": "text"}], "type": "user.message"}, "last_payload": {"item_id": "ITM-01M5EDBQP49XS17T5JW8FD0WFZ", "kind": "NEW_ITEM"}, "messages": ["b73c439110e873ec1118d851777743bfd6b9bbac65b2345b721aadd458cbc713"], "missing_fields": {}, "model_id": "gpt-6.1-sol", "model_id_basis": "RESOLVED_SESSION_AGENT", "native_execution_receipts": {"sevt_27DnGBcrljTnr5bP2lJG1": {"execution_id": "sevt_req_6f1eedbfcdd24b1f3e19764d91bffb50679442093aa50e049813bfc63356c4af_0", "id": "sevt_27DnGBcrljTnr5bP2lJG1", "processed_at": "2026-10-21T05:05:03.482Z", "stop_reason": {"event_ids": ["call_e858182ec71f45a28fb8fc9a3b488dca|fc_01c476f17d2f28a6016ad847fdeb9481918894cb6d565bcae5"], "type": "requires_action"}, "type": "session.status_idle"}, "sevt_A3_zu1tUWW978Fy5yjdX3": {"execution_id": "sevt_req_10d672489474d719f1ba810651b7a449050c182fbdb78f86e22c3abb76923a39_0", "id": "sevt_A3_zu1tUWW978Fy5yjdX3", "processed_at": "2026-10-21T05:04:12.553Z", "type": "session.status_running"}, "sevt_DfN3kJ5u4Fwe3gMBJjLkx": {"execution_id": "sevt_req_017a00695bea7568fc97dfc499a93bd26c35f6a3d2a77eb8f010f11047e4c211_0", "id": "sevt_DfN3kJ5u4Fwe